LancerFit admin console
=======================

Web console for Campus Recreation staff. Everything the student app shows is
managed here: challenges and their podium rewards, the validation queue for
supervised results, leaderboards, the daily quest bank and rotation, the
facility activity catalogue, and admin accounts.

React 19, TypeScript, Vite, React Router, axios, socket.io-client.
Staff only. There is no student-facing route.


Quick Start
-----------

	npm install
	echo "VITE_API_PATH=http://localhost:8000/api" > .env
	npm run dev              # http://localhost:5173

	npm run build            # tsc -b && vite build
	npm run preview
	npm run lint

VITE_API_PATH must end in /api. The socket origin is derived from it by
stripping that suffix, so a wrong base URL produces a console that logs in but
never updates live.


Essential Documentation
-----------------------

All maintainer documentation lives in docs/:

* docs/architecture.md    - routing, auth shell, data flow, realtime
* docs/pages.md           - what every screen does and what it calls
* docs/api-layer.md       - the client, tokens, refresh, adding a call
* docs/design-system.md   - tokens, class families, icons, avatars
* docs/operations.md      - environment, build, deployment
* docs/maintenance.md     - known gaps, dead code, traps, work queue

Read docs/architecture.md first, then docs/design-system.md before writing any
markup. The styling rules here are strict and easy to break.


Layout
------

	src/main.tsx         entry, mounts App, imports index.css
	src/App.tsx          routes and the authenticated shell
	src/index.css        the entire design system
	src/api/             axios client, socket, one folder per domain
	src/pages/           one file per route
	src/components/      shared UI
	src/context/         auth state
	public/              avatar and faculty badge PNGs served at web root


Conventions
-----------

* index.css is the only stylesheet. It is imported once, by main.tsx.
  Creating a second stylesheet is the mistake this project has already made.
* Styling is class based, using the families documented in
  docs/design-system.md. Inline style is for one-off layout only.
* No external icon library. Icons are hand-drawn SVG paths in
  components/Icon.tsx.
* No emoji in UI copy.
* Every network call goes through src/api/. Pages never call axios directly.
* A page that displays data another user can change subscribes to the
  relevant socket event and refetches.